  "title": "Kaguya MI Mineral Maps 50N-50S (Lemelin et al. 2016)",
  "description": "Abundance maps of plagioclase, olivine, orthopyroxene and clinopyroxene between 50N and 50S, derived from topographically corrected Kaguya Multiband Imager UVVIS reflectance with Hapke radiative transfer modeling (Lemelin et al. 2015, 2016, 2019). Resampled by USGS from 2048 ppd to 512 ppd (59 m/pixel), Simple Cylindrical. Source GeoTIFFs store weight fraction; the COGs store wt% in IAU:30100.",
